1
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,860
Welcome to the Breath Reset.

2
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,810
Today we're going to
practice Breathe Light,

3
00:00:13,860 --> 00:00:18,680
learning to breathe a little
quieter, softer, and more comfortably.

4
00:00:19,980 --> 00:00:21,260
Let's begin.

5
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:29,970
Gently close your eyes and allow your

6
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:34,400
sit bones to feel grounded beneath you.

7
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:41,720
Imagine a piece of string lightly
lifting you from the crown of your head.

8
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:46,550
Let your shoulders
soften and relax your jaw

9
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:54,160
and begin by simply
noticing your breathing.

10
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:59,810
Notice the air entering through
the nose, perhaps feeling

11
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:05,800
slightly cooler as it comes in
and a little warmer as it leaves.

12
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:11,620
No need to change
anything yet, just notice.

13
00:01:18,720 --> 00:01:23,560
Now begin to bring a little
softness into your breathing.

14
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:30,250
Allow the inhale to
become gentle and quiet and

15
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:35,060
as you exhale simply
allow the air to leave.

16
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:40,530
No pushing, no forcing.

17
00:01:44,510 --> 00:01:48,180
With your next breath
see if you can make the

18
00:01:48,230 --> 00:01:55,330
inhale just a little
smaller, a little softer.

19
00:01:56,460 --> 00:02:00,150
And allow the exhale to happen naturally.

20
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,410
Imagine there's a delicate feather

21
00:02:04,460 --> 00:02:07,430
resting just beneath your nose and as you

22
00:02:07,480 --> 00:02:11,850
breathe in and out see if you can breathe

23
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:17,160
so gently that the feather barely moves.

24
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:21,110
That's the quality we're looking for.

25
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:26,700
Soft, quiet, imperceptible breathing.

26
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:43,200
Now we're going to experiment
with breathing a little less air.

27
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:47,410
Not necessarily breathing
slower but taking

28
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:51,130
in a smaller amount of
air with each breath.

29
00:02:53,370 --> 00:03:00,140
Soften the inhale, relax
the exhale and then see if

30
00:03:00,190 --> 00:03:05,610
you can soften the next
inhale just a little more.

31
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:14,460
As you reduce the amount of air you're

32
00:03:14,510 --> 00:03:18,480
breathing you may begin
to notice a very slight

33
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:24,060
desire to take a big
breath, a gentle feeling

34
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:27,930
that you could do with
just a little more air.

35
00:03:28,290 --> 00:03:35,710
That's what we're exploring,
just a mild comfortable sensation.

36
00:03:45,130 --> 00:03:49,140
Continue breathing
gently through your nose,

37
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:55,950
a soft inhale and an effortless exhale.

38
00:03:56,190 --> 00:04:01,940
Notice whether you can make your
breathing just a little lighter,

39
00:04:01,990 --> 00:04:06,490
almost as though you're breathing
less air than you normally would.

40
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:16,720
And remember you don't need
to achieve anything here,

41
00:04:16,770 --> 00:04:20,650
just stay curious about what you notice.

42
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:33,190
And now slowly release any
control over your breathing.

43
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:38,330
Allow your body to breathe in
whatever rhythm feels natural.

44
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:43,590
No need to make the breath
smaller or slower anymore.

45
00:04:48,570 --> 00:04:51,410
Notice how you're feeling.

46
00:04:51,690 --> 00:04:54,290
Does your breathing feel any different?

47
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:58,560
Perhaps a little quieter or more relaxed

48
00:04:58,610 --> 00:05:03,250
or perhaps it feels exactly the same.

49
00:05:03,650 --> 00:05:06,270
Whatever you notice is okay.

50
00:05:09,730 --> 00:05:16,930
When you're ready, gently bring
your awareness back into the room.

51
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:22,350
As you go through your day, notice whether

52
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:24,890
you're breathing with
more effort than you need.

53
00:05:24,940 --> 00:05:27,450
And if it feels comfortable,
allow it to soften.

54
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:32,680
Sometimes breathing better
is simply about doing less.

